  "strategy": "In this problem, the goal is to minimize the AC1 upper bound score for sequences of nonnegative coefficients (each between 0 and 1000) using an authoritative evaluator based exclusively on self-linear convolution. The score is defined as \\(\\text{score} = \\frac{2n \\cdot \\max(\\text{convolve}(a,a))}{(\\sum a)^2}\\), where \\(n\\) is the sequence length and \\(\\text{convolve}(a,a)\\) spans \\(2n-1\\) coefficients. The previous program achieved a score of approximately 1.5095, and the target is to achieve 1.5027 or lower.\n\n**Central Idea:** This problem is approached by exploiting the duality between sequence design and its self-convolution bounded by a maximum value \\(M\\). The optimal sequence minimizes \\(\\frac{2n \\cdot M}{(\\sum a)^2}\\) while maintaining nonnegativity and the coefficient cap. Key advancements include:\n1. A homogeneity-preserving approach that fixes the sequence sum to 100 to decouple normalization\n2. Support for multiple lengths including parent-length (384) through dimension-aware checks\n3. An identity-efficient implementation focusing twin concerns:\n   - Feasible candidate sequences must satisfy \\(\\sum a \\geq 0.01\\) post-normalization\n   - Creator must distinguish valid sequences from parents when available\n4. A Lipschitz-enforced schedule that respects time deadlines with dynamic budget distribution\n5. Hybrid solution framework combining constraint-augmented optimization for stability and gradient-free exploration for flexibility\n\n**Implementation Procedure:**\n1. **Infrastructure Setup:** \nFix floating-point precision to 32-bit to accelerate calculations and copy evaluation contexts without mutation.\n\n2. **Definition of Variables:** The core solver uses three types of vectors:\n   - `base` vectors (fixed-length parent input)\n   - `candidate` vectors (of varying lengths from 72)\n   - `gradient_info` pkg (stored as mean gradient magnitude alongside normalized sequences)\n\n3. **Heuristic-Driven Initializations:**\n   - Tone coloring (audio signals) for baseline quality\n   - Randomized smoothing to penalize extreme peaks\n   - Polynomial phase perturbations to counteract solver stagnation\n\n4. **Core Optimization Loop:**\n   - **Convolution Thresholding:** For each convolution output, take the logarithm (log-binning) to better identify peaks\n   - **L1 Regularization:** Add sparsity term `1e-3 * L1_penalty` to prevent overfitting at the extreme tails\n   - **Gradient Projection:** Calculate gradient as `-derivative(score)`, clamp to [-5, 5] to prevent invalid steps\n   - **Component-Wise Android Approach:** Handle dimensions dynamically through length\ub354\ub77c\ub3c4\n namely 7 or  Children word count\n\n5. **Termination Conditions:**\n   - Keep track of best score and corresponding sequence\n   - Use hard checkpointing via budget snapshots at 30% via budget time points\n   - Sensitivity checks against the evaluator's requirements\n\n**Mathematical Voicing:** The optimization requires minimizing the AC1 score via:\n\n\\[\n\\operatorname{AC1}(a) = \\frac{2n \\cdot \\max_{i}( \\text{convolve}[a]_{i} )}{(\\sum a)^{2}}\n\\]\n\nEncoded as a homogeneous function, we can fix \\(\\sum a = 100\\) to decouple normalization. The resulting problem is:\n\n\\[\n\\min_{a \\in \\mathbb{R}_{+}^{n}, M \\in \\mathbb{R}_{+}} \\quad M\n\\]\nsubject to\n\\[\n\\text{convolve}[a]_{i} \\leq M \\quad \\forall i \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\sum_{j} a_{j} = 100\n\\]\n\n**Suggestion use:** \nList all coefficients in Python list. No file system access allowed.\n\n**Useful Out of the Box Initialization (OOB):**\nWhen no parent is available, fallback to uniform random in [0.1, 1000] for any length. When parent is available, it should be used directly for one of the seeds but must be wrapped via proper normalization.\n\nThe proposed offer includes complete steps with no need for blind repetition. To deploy this, the following provides a verified stopping property at budget thresholds.",
